The platform's mixer takes the place of m4a_1.s. Under IRV_WASM m4a.c runs it at 42048 Hz,
the highest rate of the expansion's table (704 samples per frame at 59.7275 frames per
second), and gives it the reciprocal of that rate as a float. The PSG channels have no
hardware to play them: the platform's cgb_audio.c synthesises them from the sound registers,
and it needs to hear when CgbSound and CgbOscOff start a note, set its sweep, length or
envelope, or load the wave RAM, at the places the port's m4a.c tells it.

